# Bloatmaw — a floating mass of flesh for the FPS roster. One great ball of a
# body, mostly mouth, hovering above the floor on nothing at all: the first
# legless, floorless character in the cast.
#
# THE READ, in silhouette order: a single huge sphere of wet meat hanging in
# the air; its whole front split by a maw a third of the ball's own width; a
# ring of irregular bone teeth around the opening; an ember core burning in
# the throat; two MISMATCHED eyes set unevenly above the maw; a crown of
# small swept-back spurs; and, absurd against all that bulk, two withered
# arms dangling off the flanks with broken shackles at the wrists. No legs,
# no ground contact — the hover gap is the character.
#
# FLOATING. `stance` is OMITTED on purpose (see the model block): the grammar
# knows only humanoid/digitigrade and this body has no legs at all. The maw,
# teeth, eyes and throat core are GEOMETRY (prims), not a painted decal:
# there is no reference mesh to bake, and the painted-face road has failed
# this project repeatedly (face.ts's header records four rebuilds). No sheet
# block, so the registry wears ZOMBIE_FLAT.
#
# THE MAW IS NOT A CARVE. A carve into a body this big is painted by the BALL,
# not by whatever sits in the cavity: the paint rule is arg-min of the
# primitive's signed distance, and a point on a carved wall is DEEP inside the
# ball, so the ball always wins the pixel and a dark or glowing throat prim
# inside the hole would render as plain flesh. So the maw is an additive dark
# mass that owns its own surface by protruding from the ball's front, with the
# lit core protruding further still. (Cyclops paid for the carve version: two
# carve attempts left GPU holes the CPU field did not have, 2026-08-22.)
model bloatmaw
  # height = the TOP OF THE BALL, not a standing crown. The whole body hovers:
  # ball centre y = 1.08, y-semi-axis 0.749 -> top 1.829, underside 0.302.
  # THE HOVER GAP IS 0.302 m. Move HOVER (the centre height) and re-check the
  # top against this number if the body is ever rescaled. Nothing in the
  # format enforces ground contact — there is no sole-at-y=0 rule in
  # blob-checks.ts or validate.ts — which is exactly why a floating body
  # validates cleanly at all.
  height 1.83
  # NO `stance` LINE. `checkStance` is the format's one intent check and it
  # only knows humanoid/digitigrade knees; omitting the line means "not
  # checked", which is the honest state for a body with no leg chain. A
  # defaulted intent would be a guess.

skeleton
  # THE ROOT IS THE BALL'S CENTRE, not a pelvis. `root pelvis at 1.08` puts
  # the root bone's HEAD at the hover centre; the 0.06 length is a stub up to
  # 1.14 so children hang off its tail per the grammar. The name `pelvis` is
  # inherited from the format and is a lie here — read it as "ball centre".
  root pelvis at 1.08 len=0.06

  # A vertical axis through the ball: it exists for the gait wiring (the
  # motion profile maps spine/neck/skull by name) and to hang the crown spurs
  # on. The flesh ignores it.
  bone spine parent=pelvis dir=up len=0.30          # 1.14 -> 1.44
  bone neck  parent=spine  dir=up len=0.16          # 1.44 -> 1.60
  bone skull parent=neck   dir=up len=0.14          # 1.60 -> 1.74

  # THE MAW AXIS — forward out of the ball centre to its front surface. Every
  # mouth prim (dark maw, teeth, lit core) rides this bone with an `offset=`,
  # so the whole face moves as one if the ball is rescaled.
  bone maw parent=pelvis dir=fwd len=0.70           # 1.14 -> z 0.70

  mirror
    # TINY ARMS. The clavicle does NOT run sideways: it runs DOWN-OUT at 63
    # degrees so the shoulder seats near the ball's EQUATOR, where the surface
    # is at x 0.62 — an arm rooted higher or lower sits deep inside a sphere
    # that has barely curved in, and gets no daylight (the goblin lesson: the
    # lever on arm clearance is the BODY's width, not the arm's).
    # Shoulder lands at (0.633, 1.118); the ball surface there is x 0.618, so
    # the 0.085 shoulder ball is welded in by ~7 cm and pokes out by ~10 cm.
    bone clavicle parent=spine    dir=down tilt=63 len=0.71
    bone upperArm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=60 len=0.13
    bone foreArm  parent=upperArm dir=down tilt=50 pitch=8 len=0.11
    bone hand     parent=foreArm  dir=down tilt=45 pitch=10 len=0.07
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # THE BALL — one great hanging meat balloon. Three blended masses: the
  # main ellipsoid carries the silhouette, the other two fatten the crown
  # and the underside so it reads as a sagging organ rather than a pool
  # ball. `core` marks the main mass for the fuse probe.
  # ============================================================
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 r=0.720 wide=0.86 tall=1.04 deep=1.00 blend=0.030 core
  # Upper swell: the balloon's shoulders, x-semi 0.60 at y 1.17.
  blob torso on spine  at=0.10 r=0.600 wide=0.86 tall=0.92 deep=0.92 blend=0.045
  # Lower sag: the heavy underside, dropped 0.30 and squashed tall. This is
  # what sets the 0.302 hover gap.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(0,-0.30,0) r=0.520 wide=0.86 tall=0.92 deep=0.90 blend=0.045
  # FLESHY IRREGULARITY: three off-centre swells that poke a couple of
  # centimetres proud of the ball, so the silhouette is a sagging organ rather
  # than a perfect sphere (a perfect sphere reads as a prop). Blends are loose
  # (0.04) so they merge into the mass instead of reading as separate lumps.
  blob torso on spine  at=0.42 offset=(0.34,0.06,0.14) r=0.170 wide=1.15 tall=0.95 deep=1.15 blend=0.040
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(-0.36,-0.16,0.10) r=0.160 wide=1.10 tall=1.00 deep=1.10 blend=0.040
  blob torso on spine  at=0.15 offset=(0.05,0.10,-0.34) r=0.180 wide=1.00 tall=1.00 deep=1.00 blend=0.045

  # ============================================================
  # THE MAW — the whole front of the ball. A wide dark mass bulging ~5 cm
  # proud of the ball's front so it OWNS its pixels (see the header: a carved
  # cavity would belong to the ball). Footprint 1.00 m wide x 0.65 m tall on
  # a ball 1.24 m wide — a third of the body. color 180406 is near-black
  # blood: the deepColor of a mouth, not a paint region.
  # ============================================================
  blob head on maw at=0.92 offset=(0,-0.09,0) r=0.44 wide=1.14 tall=0.74 deep=0.22 blend=0.012 color=180406
  # A dull ember haze in the throat, just proud of the maw so it owns a ring.
  blob head on maw at=0.94 offset=(0,-0.09,0.05) r=0.24 wide=1.15 tall=0.85 deep=0.55 blend=0.030 color=7a1404 glow=0.35
  # THE LIT CORE: a burning ember in the middle of the maw, protruding ~7 cm
  # past the dark mass so it is the outermost prim there and can glow. One
  # strong light on the character; the colour IS the emission (glow rides the
  # prim's own colour, per the grammar).
  blob head on maw at=0.94 offset=(0,-0.09,0.07) r=0.15 wide=1.05 tall=0.95 deep=1.00 blend=0.020 color=ff5a10 glow=0.95

  # ---- TEETH — irregular, none repeated -------------------------------
  # Upper row: five fangs hanging off the top lip. Bases sit on the dark
  # maw's own rim (z 0.62 is inside the maw lens at these x/y), tips point
  # down-forward so they cross the dark mass and read against it. Sizes and
  # angles deliberately uneven: 0.048/0.060/0.055/0.056/0.045.
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(-0.28,0.20,0.00) r=0.048 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(0.03,-0.26,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(-0.14,0.25,0.00) r=0.060 r2=0.009 blend=0.005 tip=(-0.02,-0.30,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(0.00,0.27,0.00) r=0.055 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(0.00,-0.32,0.23) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(0.15,0.25,0.00) r=0.056 r2=0.009 blend=0.005 tip=(0.02,-0.29,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(0.29,0.19,0.00) r=0.045 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(-0.03,-0.25,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  # Lower row: four chunky stubs jutting up from the bottom lip.
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(-0.26,-0.30,0.00) r=0.050 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(0.02,0.24,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(-0.09,-0.34,0.00) r=0.058 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(0.00,0.27,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(0.10,-0.33,0.00) r=0.048 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(0.00,0.25,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(0.27,-0.29,0.00) r=0.054 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(-0.02,0.23,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55

  # ---- EYES — deliberately NOT a pair --------------------------------
  # Right eye (the character's right, +x): the big one, set HIGH, a COLD
  # pale blue — cold on purpose, so it never blurs into the orange throat.
  # Ball front at (0.25, 1.56) is z 0.470; the 0.105 eye sits at z 0.63, so
  # it bulges ~0.16 m proud and owns its pixels.
  # A dark socket ring sits BEHIND each eye so the glow reads as an eye set
  # in flesh rather than a lamp stuck on the ball; the eye protrudes further,
  # so it keeps the centre and the socket shows as a rim.
  blob head on maw at=0.72 offset=(0.25,0.42,-0.04) r=0.140 wide=1.05 tall=1.05 deep=0.85 blend=0.010 color=260a06
  blob head on maw at=0.80 offset=(0.25,0.42,0.07) r=0.105 wide=0.95 tall=0.95 deep=1.00 blend=0.006 color=bfe8ff glow=0.85
  # Heavy brow over the big eye: a flesh shelf that shades its top third.
  blob head on maw at=0.78 offset=(0.25,0.50,0.00) r=0.120 wide=1.15 tall=0.40 deep=0.95 blend=0.008
  # Left eye: smaller, lower and further out, a sick green — the mismatch is
  # the point (a neat pair on a sphere reads as a smiley face).
  blob head on maw at=0.70 offset=(-0.32,0.36,-0.06) r=0.100 wide=1.05 tall=1.00 deep=0.85 blend=0.010 color=260a06
  blob head on maw at=0.77 offset=(-0.32,0.36,0.05) r=0.070 wide=1.00 tall=0.90 deep=1.00 blend=0.005 color=a8c24a glow=0.75
  # Half-lid over the small eye: a flesh mass eating its top half, so the two
  # eyes do not even read as the same shape.
  blob head on maw at=0.75 offset=(-0.32,0.41,0.01) r=0.085 wide=1.10 tall=0.50 deep=1.00 blend=0.006

  # ---- CROWN SPURS — small, swept back, uneven ------------------------
  # Three pairs (`both`) rooted in the ball's crown and raked back so the
  # tips trail toward -z; none rises above the declared height (tallest tip
  # y 1.80 against the ball's 1.829 top).
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0.09,0.08,-0.06) r=0.038 r2=0.004 blend=0.005 chamfer tip=(0.02,0.03,-0.30) both color=6b5a44
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0.26,0.05,-0.04) r=0.034 r2=0.004 blend=0.005 chamfer tip=(0.04,0.02,-0.28) both color=6b5a44
  blob head on skull at=0.70 offset=(0.15,0.07,-0.10) r=0.030 r2=0.004 blend=0.005 chamfer tip=(0.03,0.02,-0.22) both color=6b5a44

  # ============================================================
  # THE ARMS — withered, too weak to matter, ending in little grasping
  # hands. One mass per segment plus a palm and two fingers.
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on clavicle at=1.00 r=0.085 blend=0.014 mirror core
  bar  arm on upperArm from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.048 r2=0.036 blend=0.010 mirror
  blob arm on upperArm at=1.00 r=0.044 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  arm on foreArm  from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.038 r2=0.028 blend=0.008 mirror
  # Palm: a small flat mitt, widened across x.
  blob arm on hand at=0.55 r=0.044 wide=1.15 tall=0.85 deep=1.15 blend=0.008 mirror
  # Two crooked fingers, splayed by their own x offsets (under mirror the .r
  # copy reflects offset.x, so each hand gets a two-finger fan).
  bar arm on hand from=0.80 to=1.18 r=0.015 r2=0.005 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.028,0.010,0.018) tip=(0.010,-0.046,0.038) mirror
  bar arm on hand from=0.78 to=1.10 r=0.013 r2=0.004 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(-0.024,0.004,0.010) tip=(-0.008,-0.040,0.030) mirror

# Face block: SHRUNK TO A NUB. The ball is the head, so the parameterised
# skull ellipsoid would sit a zombie head inside it; headRadius 0.001 kills
# it and the brow/nose gates (0) emit nothing. Same idiom as gargoyle.blob.
# No `sheet` block: there is no reference mesh to bake and no hand-authored
# decal is shipped, so the registry wears ZOMBIE_FLAT.
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.006
  headRise   0
  headLead   0

# Diseased wet flesh: a dark raw-meat base that the shader sRGB-encodes much
# lighter than these numbers read, a red wound interior, and a bile-yellow
# mottle that differs in HUE from the base (a same-hue darker mottle is
# invisible). Wetness high — this thing is slimy — with a soft sheen rather
# than a hard specular.
palette
  baseColor     0.30 0.15 0.12
  deepColor     0.55 0.09 0.07
  charColor     0.07 0.05 0.04
  specIntensity 0.50
  specRoughness 0.34
  fresnelBoost  0.35
  translucency  0.16
  wetness       0.60
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.06
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.02
  mottleAmp     0.50
  mottleScale   2.4
  mottleColor   0.24 0.26 0.09
